    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nAs a user, I want to be able to specify which command, the \"mini.files\" module uses to delete a file/folder, so that when i delete a file it moves the file to the system trash can or recycle bin.\r\n\r\n* Given that i am on a MacOS computer, i want to be able to use the [trash](https://hasseg.org/trash/) command.\r\n* Given that i am on Windows computer, i want to be able to use the [recycle.exe](https://github.com/kizzx2/cmd-recycle) command.\r\n* Given that i am on Linux computer, i want to be able to use the [trash-put](https://github.com/andreafrancia/trash-cli.git) from the trash cli.\r\n\r\n### Proposal\r\n\r\nIn the `mini.files` module:\r\n* Add a `config.options.delete_command` to the default config as an empty string. \r\n* Update `H.fs_delete` function in the `mini.files` arguments to `function(path, permanent_delete, delete_command)`\r\n* Pass `config.options.delete_command` into `delete_command` argument\r\n* Update `H.fs_delete` function in the `mini.files` module to check if `delete_command` is empty\r\n* When `delete_command` is not empty call `os.execute(delete_command .. ' ' .. path)`\r\n\r\n### Additional Notes\r\n\r\nI have tested this locally and it seems to work fine. I intend to make a pull request, after i have check my changes against to CONTRIBUTING.md guidelines. \r\n\r\nI welcome any feedback, questions, or comments.",
