            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I also just started using this plugin and was looking for an answer to this.\n\nCollecting the reasons from you to not add it from the different threads linked here and then recursively:\n> Basically: too complex to do it right and cross-platform.\n\nnothing to say about this since it doesn't really say anything specific\n\n> Also having a way to customize deleting but not other actions seems a bit off, which only adds to the complexity/maintenance.\n\nthere is an extra option now either way so this is no longer relevant.\n\n> My main reason for not going with delete_cmd is mostly because it is virtually Unix-only; Windows users probably won't install any CLI apps.\n\nthat doesn't make sense, like just because it's more unlikely that windows users will use this is no reason to not add it\n\n\n\nSo either I missed something or there weren't really any good reasons for not adding this. It should be as simple as `vim.system(user_cmd:format(file))` (or however you pass the file to the user cmd added at this line https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.files/blob/02874bc653fbecf2bee2c65441d0ebd09110f011/lua/mini/files.lua#L2955",
