            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> So either I missed something or there weren't really any good reasons for not adding this. \n\nWhat makes a reason \"good\" is in the eye of the beholder. Adding a feature that depends on three different OS specific CLI tools is not something I'd like to maintain. Even adding a placeholder config for this would require documenting how to make it useful for users, which is also maintaining (since it'll require documenting and recommending specific tools).\n\n> there is an extra option now either way so this is no longer relevant.\n> ...\n> It should be as simple as `vim.system(user_cmd:format(file))` (or however you pass the file to the user cmd added at this line https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.files/blob/02874bc653fbecf2bee2c65441d0ebd09110f011/lua/mini/files.lua#L2955\n\nThe `user_cmd` is another extra option, though.\n\n> A really easy way to get this working for at least some users would be to just allow to configure the trash directory I guess.\n\nThis is not as easy as that, since deleting to trash directory is special. There has to be some metadata stored about files for them to be able to be restored. That's the reasons there are OS specific tools that take care of this.",
